# Draw a PNG image with the plotter pen.
#
# The file must resolve inside the configured image_dir or output_dir.
# Paths outside those roots, unsupported suffixes, and missing files are
# rejected before any image processing.
#
# Pipeline (SDK/robonix_sdk/{image,trajectory}.py):
#   grayscale -> Otsu threshold (or `threshold`) -> marching-squares
#   outlines -> Douglas-Peucker (simplify_px) -> pen-up/down waypoints.
#
# Orientation:
#   orientation = "" / "auto" (default)
#       Honour Robonix metadata embedded by render_preview. Such PNGs are
#       drawn screen-upright and at their stored millimetre scale. PNGs
#       without metadata are drawn screen-upright too (the way the file is
#       displayed) and auto-fit to the paper.
#   orientation = "screen"
#       Force screen-upright (flip_y=true), regardless of metadata.
#   orientation = "paper"
#       Force the raw raster mapping (flip_y=false), regardless of metadata.
#   flip_x always mirrors left/right. flip_y mirrors the screen orientation
#   top/bottom; it is only consulted when orientation is auto and the PNG
#   has no orientation metadata.
#   Rotation is not a parameter: rotate the image file beforehand.
#
# trace selects how ink becomes pen paths:
#   "outline"   trace the boundary of the ink (marching squares). Correct
#               for silhouettes and filled shapes; a drawn line becomes
#               two parallel sides.
#   "skeleton"  trace the centreline of the ink (Zhang-Suen thinning).
#               Best for line art: one pen stroke per drawn line.
#   "lineart"   extract edges with a difference-of-Gaussians filter, keep
#               weak edges connected to strong ones (hysteresis), then
#               skeletonise. Best for photos and grey artwork; threshold
#               is not used in this mode, invert still selects polarity.
#   "" / "auto" use the skill config; auto picks "skeleton" for PNGs made
#               by render_preview (they carry Robonix metadata) and
#               "outline" otherwise.
#   lineart sigma/detail, spur length and minimum contour length come from
#   the skill config (trace_lineart_sigma, trace_lineart_detail,
#   trace_spur_px, trace_min_length_mm). Fragments whose endpoints are
#   within trace_bridge_px pixels are joined into one continuous stroke.
#
# scale:
#   < 0  force automatic fit-to-paper (ignores metadata scale)
#   = 0  use metadata pixel_to_mm when present, otherwise auto-fit
#   > 0  explicit pixel-to-millimetre factor, using offset_x/offset_y as
#        the placement origin in millimetres
#
# offset_x/offset_y: when both are 0 and the PNG carries Robonix
# metadata, the metadata offsets are used. A generated PNG normally has
# offset 0, so the drawing starts at the workspace origin.
#
# threshold <= 0 selects Otsu. invert=true traces light ink on a dark
# background. simplify_px = 0 disables simplification; negative uses the
# skill config. fill <= 0 and margin_mm < 0 use the skill config.
# margin_mm/fill apply only to automatic fitting.
#
# Leave workspace.x_max <= workspace.x_min (the default) to use the
# configured workspace. When supplied, workspace.z_up <= z_down falls
# back to the configured pen heights.
#
# The global motion profile (velocity/acceleration/deceleration/jerk,
# pen heights) is owned by the plotter primitive and is not a parameter
# here: change it with plotter_set_params. This tool never calls
# SET_PARAM, so user-selected values persist across draws.
string  image_path
string  orientation
string  trace
float64 scale
float64 offset_x
float64 offset_y
float64 threshold
bool    invert
bool    flip_x
bool    flip_y
float64 simplify_px
float64 fill
float64 margin_mm
# Plan only: return point count, do not move the machine.
bool    dry_run
# Run the primitive HOME routine after a successful draw.
bool    auto_home
# The pilot already homed before this call; do not repeat HOME.
bool    skip_home
plot/Workspace workspace
---
bool    success
string  message
uint32  points
# Resolved absolute path inside image_dir/output_dir.
string  image_path
# Effective pixel-to-mm factor used for this draw.
float64 pixel_to_mm
# Effective vertical orientation after metadata/orientation resolution.
bool    flip_y
# Effective tracing mode: outline, skeleton or lineart.
string  trace
float64 min_x
float64 max_x
float64 min_y
float64 max_y
float64 elapsed_s